-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",456,{
[14561]="70048CA4\n1\tCollect guano piles (total: 10)\tGuano piles can be found in the Lair of the Gloom-lord. You should collect guano piles because Viznak asked.\n2\tTalk to Viznak after completing Surveying Seregost\tViznak can be found outside of Seregost once you have completed Surveying Seregost. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[14562]="70018E3E\n1\tDefeat Frost-wolves (total: 4)\030Defeat Grizzled Frost-wolves (total: 2)\tWolves can be found by the frozen lake, north-east of Frerin's Court. Nos Grimsong has asked you to thin the number of wolves in the region.\n2\tTalk to Nos Grimsong in Frerin's Court\tNos Grimsong is in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court. You should return to Nos Grimsong for your reward.\n",
[14563]="70025B50\n1\tSpeak with Avery Crabapple during the Flower-blooming Season\tAvery Crabapple is in the Market Square of Bree. You should speak with Avery Crabapple, as you have been asked to help him with a very difficult task during the flower-blooming season.\n",
[14564]="7002C675\n1\tDefeat Oathbreaker champions (total: 8)\030Defeat Oathbreaker archers (total: 8)\tThe Oathbreakers of Parth Celebrant can be found to the north, east, and west of Idmar's camp. Idmar has asked you to banish the shades from Parth Celebrant.\n2\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should return to Idmar with news of your success.\n",
[14565]="7001B253\n1\tExamine engraved stones (total: 5)\tThe barrows are in the eastern reaches of the Scuttledells, north-east of Ivorel's camp. Ivorel has asked you to study the stones in the barrows, looking for any engravings that might describe their history and give some clue as to the nature of the threat they contain.\n2\tTalk to Ivorel\tIvorel's camp is south-west of the barrows. You should return to Ivorel with the engraved stones you found.\n",
[14566]="70041177\n1\tDefeat Ruthless Oathbreakers in Tarlang's Crown (total: 3)\030Defeat Ruthless Bowmen in Tarlang's Crown (total: 3)\030Defeat Ruthless Warriors in Tarlang's Crown (total: 2)\tThe Dead can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown. You have encountered the Ruthless Dead and should defeat them before they can be wielded against the people of Gondor.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Dead in Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[14567]="7003E458\n1\tSearch for Treebeard in Fangorn Forest\tAccording to Quickbeam's Huorn, Treebeard must be somewhere in Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam's Huorn wants to search for Treebeard as he could be of great help in maintaining order in the forest. You should aid the Huorn.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found in Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn. Quickbeam's Huorn has found no sign of Treebeard. As its agitation has not subsided by now, you should bring him to Quickbeam and have him explain where Treebeard has gone.\n",
[14568]="7006300F\n1\tHide hobbit prints (total: 6)\tHeleth Bach has asked you to smooth over and hide any tracks that she may have left behind down by the river. The river is north-west of Lintrev, in southern Swanfleet.\n2\tReturn to Heleth\tYou should let Heleth know that you have hidden her tracks. Heleth Bach is in Lintrev.\n",
[14569]="700306C4\n1\tSomething near Greenroot has made him sad, but he has no memory to impress upon you. You should investigate nearby to see what has caused this Ent to wither under such a heavy cloud.\t\n2\tTell Greenroot you wish to help\tGreenroot is outside of the entrance to the Black Heart in Fangorn. You should return to Greenroot to tell him that you understand his pain, and wish to help if you possibly can.\n",
[14570]="7000EED9\n1\tFind the mammoth that was speared by Sigrík\tThe mammoth should be found somewhere south of Zigilgund. Sigrík has asked you to find his missing spear, which should be stuck in the corpse of a mammoth. He asked you to collect one of its tusks as well.\n2\tBring the tusk and spear back to Sigrík\tSigrík is at Zigilgund, north of the mammoth's corpse. You should return the spear and tusk to Sigrík.\n",
[14571]="7002BFF5\n1\tBring the statue to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor. You should bring the statue to Céola at once.\n",
[14572]="700717A0\n1\tReach Mokh Grazádh\tTálbiral has asked that you head south from Laivárth to an Orc camp called Mokh Grazádh and look for signs that they may be spreading the blight.\n2\tKill Orcs in Mokh Grazádh (total: 8)\030Inspect Orc supplies (total: 5)\tTálbiral has asked that you head south from Laivárth to an Orc camp called Mokh Grazádh and look for signs that they may be spreading the blight.\n3\tReturn to Tálbiral in Laivárth\tReturn to Tálbiral in Laivárth and let him know what you discovered of the Orcs plans in Mokh Grazádh.\n",
[14573]="70021AD6\n1\tPatrol Cartrev Hamon\030Patrol Cartrev Emlun\030Patrol Cartrev Rurith\030Patrol Cartrev Matho\tThe cartrevs of the Uch-lûth lie to the south of Lhanuch. Neirin Brehur has asked you to seek out the cartrevs of his people and learn if any survived the attacks of the half-orcs.\n2\tTalk to Neirin Brehur\tNeirin Brehur is at Lhanuch, north of the cartrevs. You should return to Neirin Brehur with news of your discoveries.\n",
[14574]="70071756\n1\tTravel to the Hill of the Mother\tTálbiral has given you samples of the blight gathered in Laivárth and fears that the grove is succumbing to the blight. Bring the samples to Irsinith at the Hill of the Mother as she may be able to help.\n2\tSpeak with Irsinith\tYou have arrived at the Hill of the Mother. Speak with Irsinith and show her the blight samples Tálbiral gave you from Laivárth.\n",
[14575]="7000AE52\n1\tPlace the first egg in the proper nest\tFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in yard at Sandson's farm. Wald Sandson has asked you to return the eggs for him, so that he will not get caught. You need to place the eggs back in the order they were taken, starting with the first. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tPlace the second egg in the proper nest\tFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm. Place the second egg in the proper nest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tPlace the third egg in the proper nest\tFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm. Place the third egg in the proper nest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tPlace the fourth egg in the proper nest\tFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm. Place the fourth egg in the proper nest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tPlace the fifth egg in the proper nest\tFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm. Place the fifth egg in the proper nest. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tTalk to Wald Sandson\030Collect Farmer Sandson's Notes\030Collect Basket of eggs\tWald Sandson can be found at Sandson's Farm, north and east of Michel Delving. Having replaced all the eggs, you should return and speak with Wald Sandson.\n",
[14576]="7002C59D\n1\tHelp Tatwine to better tend the horses\030Help Sabert deal with the threat of vicious dogs in the plains\tSabert guards the north gate of Stangard, and Tatwine tends the stable near the Mead Hall, in Eorlsmead. You should assist Sabert and Tatwine with anything they might need that can be done without interference from Sithric.\n2\tTell Gadda of your successes in Stangard\tGadda is near the Mead Hall in Stangard.\n",
[14577]="7004A38B\n1\tTalk to Barathron\tYou should talk to Barathron in the Foothold camp in Udûn to learn more about the riddle he wishes to solve.\n2\tYou should look for signal flags in the western half of the Udûn basin.\t\n3\tReturn to the lying slave\tThe Nurnhoth slave is lying on the southern edge of the Udûn basin, up atop a wooden structure. You should return to the slave of Nurn you found by the signal flag.\n",
[14578]="700718E6\n1\tEnter the Crypts of Gadim-ûn\tGíshgi is still distressed by the presence of the Dead in An Shêru and has asked you to re-enter the crypt below to see if you can find any explanation as to why they aren't at rest in their graves. The entrance to the Crypts of Gadim-ûn is at the north-western end of the hall.\n2\tSearch for a clue to the east\tGíshgi is still distressed by the presence of the Dead in An Shêru and has asked you to re-enter the crypt below to see if you can find any explanation as to why they aren't at rest in their graves. You should head east and search the crypts for anything notable.\n3\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have found a corrupted corpse surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Perhaps you should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n4\tSearch for another clue further east\tAfter finding a corrupted corpse, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should continue east and search the crypts for anything else notable.\n5\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have found another corrupted corpse. You should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers, as you did last time.\n6\tSearch for another clue to the south\tAfter finding two corrupted corpses, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should travel south and continue searching the crypts.\n7\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have discovered a third corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n8\tSearch for another clue to the west\tYou have now found three corrupted corpses, each surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Each time, you were able to dispel the foul voice with a lighthearted song. You should travel west and continue searching the crypts.\n9\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have yet another corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n10\tTalk to Gíshgi\tYou have found a total of four corrupted corpses, each surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Each time, you were able to dispel the foul voice with a lighthearted song. You should return to Gíshgi in Gadim-ûn and tell her what you found.\n",
[14579]="700455E1\n1\tTalk to Ulf\tUlf is at his camp within the War-stead of the King's Men. Burnoth has asked you to speak to Ulf about a plan he has devised to uncover more information about Léofdag's killer.\n2\tCollect spoils and gold from Variags in Taur Drúadan (total: 8)\tVariags can be found at the Eastern Blockade in Taur Drúadan. Ulf has asked you to recover stolen gold and spoils of war from the Variags in hopes that he might barter for information with one of their number.\n3\tDeliver the spoils to Ulf beyond the Eastern Blockade\tUlf can be found beyond the Eastern Blockade in Taur Drúadan. Ulf has asked you to meet him beyond the Eastern Blockade between the Variag and Orc forces in hopes that he might barter with one of the Variags.\n4\tTalk to Burnoth at his camp in Taur Drúadan\tBurnoth can be found at his camp among the War-stead of the King's Men in in Taur Drúadan. You aided Ulf in recovering vital information from the Variag lord, and should now report back to Burnoth before continuing your journey.\n",
[14580]="7004E1DE\n1\tTalk to Galadriel at Dol Dhannen\tGaladriel is standing before Dol Dhannen. You have travelled to the ruins of Dol Guldur, now named Dol Dhannen, with Galadriel and her company. You should speak to her before beginning your search for Karazgar.\n2\tExplore Dol Dhannen and find a way into the depths of Gostador\tGostador lies beneath the ruins of Dol Dhannen. You have come to Dol Dhannen and should now seek a way into Gostador.\n3\tEnter the trap-door and search for Karazgar in Gostador\tA weathered trap-door lies in the ruins of Dol Dhannen. You found a weather trap-door leading into Gostador. You should descend into Gostador beneath Dol Dhannen and search for Karazgar.\n4\tTalk to Galadriel at Dol Dhannen\tGaladriel can be found within Dol Dhannen. You have witnessed more of the shadowy impressions left upon the chamber by Sauron's evil and should now return to Galadriel.\n5\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain in Erebor. You have discovered that Karazgar did not return to Dol Guldur, but instead shadowy visions of his past remained among the lingering evils of Sauron within Gostador. You should return to King Thorin III and warn him that Karazgar may still lurk near to Erebor.\n",
[14581]="70049127\n1\tDefeat shadowy beings gathered in the Ered Lithui\tYou should defeat shadowy beings gathered in the Ered Lithui.\n2\tDefeat Shadow Grims in the Ered Lithui (total: 4)\030Defeat Fell Spirits in the Ered Lithui (total: 8)\030Defeat wraiths in the Ered Lithui (total: 4)\tYou should defeat shadowy beings gathered in the Ered Lithui.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeat many shadowy beings gathered in the Ered Lithui.\n",
[14582]="7004A8D8\n1\tEavesdrop on Orc-trackers in Rath Cail\030Eavesdrop on Orc-trackers near Kála-murg\030Eavesdrop on Orc-trackers near Lugvarg\tOrc-trackers can be found throughout Rath Cail, near the Orc-hold of Kála-murg, and near the watch-tower of Lugvarg. Legolas has asked you to eavesdrop on the Orcs in Rath Cail to learn more of what has happened in Lhingris since Sauron's fall. NOTE: You must select at least one of the gathered Orcs at each location to advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Legolas in Rath Cail\tLegolas can be found in the northern reaches of Rath Cail. You have carefully overheard the conversations of the Orc-trackers of Lhingris and should now return to Legolas.\n",
[14583]="70067F52\n1\tSpeak with Ayaluk and complete 'Instance: Whispers of the Forge'\tAyaluk asked you to meet him near the entry of the overseer's office.\n2\tTalk to Ayaluk\tAfter assisting Ayaluk he returned to his family home with haste. He directed you to speak with him there.\n",
[14584]="70055055\n1\tDeliver the disgusting filth to a collection box\030Collect disgusting filth (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire disgusting filth.\n",
[14585]="70055058\n1\tDeliver the night-touched furs to a collection box\030Collect night-touched furs (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire night-touched furs.\n",
[14586]="70055056\n1\tDeliver the toughened skins to a collection box\030Collect toughened skins (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire toughened skins.\n",
[14587]="70055054\n1\tDeliver the tufted ears to a collection box\030Collect tufted ears (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire tufted ears.\n",
[14588]="70062F1E\n1\tSpeak with the White Hand emissary\tYou may accept the blessing of the White Hand. Renounce the other clans and choose to stand with the White Hand.\n",
[14589]="70028445\n1\tThe Pillar of the Hand lies to the east of Dagoras' camp. Dagoras has asked you to intercept a Dunlending messenger as he passes by the Pillar of the Hand. You should first eliminate the sentries by the Pillar.\t\n2\tTalk to Dagoras at his camp in Nan Curunír\tDagoras is encamped near the entrance to Nan Curunír, west of the Pillar of the Hand. You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.\n",
[14590]="70015E12\n1\tTalk to Ornras at Echad Mirobel\tEchad Mirobel is west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road. You have been instructed to warn Echad Mirobel of the White Hand threat.\n",
[14591]="700413C7\n1\tEnter the Orc encampment.\tThe Orc camp of Gríshru is located in the north-eastern part of Ringló Vale. You should enter Gríshru.\n2\tDefeat Cave Trolls (total: 3)\030Defeat the White Mountain captain\tThe Orc forces can be found in the Orc camp, Gríshru. Defeat the Orc forces.\n3\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tSpeak with Arvaethor.\n",
[14592]="70035856\n1\tDestroy traps (total: 8)\tTraps can be found on the icy plains of the central Whitshaws. You should destroy the traps laid by the Orcs.\n2\tReturn to Ealswith\tEalswith is in Forlaw. You should return to Ealswith.\n",
})
